#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-extract-structure.bpmn:66
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owner, 2026-11-11 (who-iris, card Q-ODD-1 = A): \"force OCR when a page's text layer fails a quality check\". A text layer can hold plenty of letters and still not be the page's text: accents mapped to Greek letters (\"dΘclaration\"), Persian set in the wrong Arabic code points, words split by kerning (\"au g m ente\"), fake-bold words printed twice, mojibake. cat-harness-tools scripts/_text_quality.py checks every page against the document's languages (dc.language.iso, or --lang-hint); the router then OCRs the document and pdf-structure.py --ocr takes the OCR text for the failing pages only, listing them in structure.json source.ocr_pages with the reason. When most pages of a document with no outline fail, the whole document is read from OCR, as for a scan. Method: skill l1-document-ingestion, \"A text layer that is not text\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-extract-structure.bpmn:81
#. Diagram label
msgid "Split into sections/*.md with doc_brief front-matter"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-extract-structure.bpmn:107
#. Diagram label
msgid "Structured"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-extract-structure.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The document has a text layer: extract it with pdf-extract (pdfminer.six, then a zero-dependency content-stream reader). Exit 2 means no text layer — a scan — and routes to OCR; it is not an empty document."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-extract-structure.bpmn:34
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Two provenance paths converge on the same Task_Sections output — an embedded text layer extracted directly, or OCR that leaves the fuller text in ocr/ with only a stub in sections/ — and which branch this lane took is invisible downstream except to a grep that knows to check the fourth tier. Task_Candidates stays a proposal: nothing downstream may treat it as an adjudicated verdict."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-extract-structure.bpmn:91
#. Diagram label
msgid "Write structure.json"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-extract-structure.bpmn:92
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Write structure.json (pdf-structure/v1): doc id, TOC from the PDF outline or inferred from headings, page ranges, metadata, and source{} with the sha256 and a mimetype sniffed from the bytes, never the extension. A structure that could not be determined says so in structure_note rather than being rendered as one. For OCR'd text, source.runContext cites the OCR step's run context by sha256. A title already known for the document (the catalogue's dc.title, or one given with --title) is passed through as the raw title, so the sections' doc_title does not carry a scan's misreading."
msgstr ""

